            "<p>Parallel Circuit</p>",
            "<p>Components connected in multiple paths</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "rdtbwws",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Magnetism"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3c5x0zr",
      "content": "Magnetism is the property of materials that attract iron and other magnetic materials."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wa4eqtz",
      "content": "Magnets have two poles: North pole and South pole."
    },
    {
      "id": "wkzu0mm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Properties of Magnets"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wzaevjl",
      "content": "• Like poles repel each other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hy1fmh5",
      "content": "• Unlike poles attract each other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2djt5m3",
      "content": "• Magnetic poles always exist in pairs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mzxmz40",
      "content": "• Magnetic force is strongest at the poles."
    },
    {
      "id": "en0rj79",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Electromagnet"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lglxeqs",
      "content": "An electromagnet is a magnet produced by passing electric current through a coil of wire."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lu7wx9m",
      "content": "Applications:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "In a series circuit, current remains the same throughout, but total voltage is divided among components.",
        "In a parallel circuit, voltage across all branches is identical, but total current splits among branches.",
        "Soft iron is used to make electromagnets due to high retentivity and low coercivity, whereas steel is used for permanent magnets.",
        "Safety fuses are always connected in series with the live wire and have low melting points."
      ],
      "id": "3a4250j"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "iaporf6",
      "content": "• Electric bell"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "kk681gm",
      "content": "• Electric motors"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "00xe629",
      "content": "• Magnetic cranes"
    },
    {
      "id": "c3qxp5i",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c6jq1dp",
      "content": "• SI unit of electric current is Ampere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xr18u6u",
      "content": "• Ohm’s law formula is V = IR."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t7yydm5",
      "content": "• SI unit of resistance is Ohm."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "osf76vl",
      "content": "• Like poles repel and unlike poles attract."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}